1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,146
Dry, rubbery chicken breast?

2
00:00:02,380 --> 00:00:03,435
It's not you.

3
00:00:03,726 --> 00:00:04,886
It's the method.

4
00:00:05,851 --> 00:00:08,000
Here are seven steps to chicken that is

5
00:00:08,010 --> 00:00:12,619
juicy, tender and safe, every single time.

6
00:00:13,072 --> 00:00:15,744
And stay for step six: it's the one

7
00:00:15,754 --> 00:00:17,843
that ends the guessing for good.

8
00:00:18,467 --> 00:00:19,372
WikiTube.

9
00:00:19,547 --> 00:00:21,775
Whatever it is, here's how.

10
00:00:22,067 --> 00:00:25,354
Chicken breast has almost no fat, so there

11
00:00:25,364 --> 00:00:26,884
is very little margin.

12
00:00:27,547 --> 00:00:31,612
Two things dry it out: uneven thickness,
and

13
00:00:31,622 --> 00:00:33,049
cooking it too long.

14
00:00:33,595 --> 00:00:35,965
We'll fix both, then add a quick salt

15
00:00:35,975 --> 00:00:39,414
brine for extra moisture, and a
thermometer, the

16
00:00:39,424 --> 00:00:42,139
only reliable way to know it's done.

17
00:00:42,700 --> 00:00:45,848
You'll need boneless chicken breasts, salt
and pepper,

18
00:00:45,858 --> 00:00:48,434
a skillet with a lid, a meat thermometer,

19
00:00:48,493 --> 00:00:50,779
and a meat mallet or a rolling pin.

20
00:00:50,954 --> 00:00:52,416
Plus a little oil.

21
00:00:52,967 --> 00:00:53,999
Step one.

22
00:00:54,546 --> 00:00:57,101
Place the chicken breast between two
sheets of

23
00:00:57,111 --> 00:01:00,396
plastic wrap or baking paper on a cutting
board.

24
00:01:01,361 --> 00:01:03,917
Using a mallet, a rolling pin or the

25
00:01:03,927 --> 00:01:06,726
bottom of a heavy pan, gently pound the

26
00:01:06,736 --> 00:01:09,315
thickest part until the whole breast is
about

27
00:01:09,325 --> 00:01:13,295
three quarters of an inch, or two
centimetres, thick.

28
00:01:14,260 --> 00:01:16,595
Don't pound it into a pancake, because you

29
00:01:16,605 --> 00:01:18,357
just want an even shape.

30
00:01:18,718 --> 00:01:21,273
Equal thickness means the whole piece
cooks at

31
00:01:21,283 --> 00:01:25,160
the same speed, which is the key to juicy
results.

32
00:01:26,310 --> 00:01:28,611
Very large breasts can also be cut in

33
00:01:28,621 --> 00:01:33,241
half horizontally to make two thinner
cutlets, which cook faster.

34
00:01:33,800 --> 00:01:34,844
Step two.

35
00:01:35,135 --> 00:01:38,582
Dissolve two tablespoons of salt in four
cups,

36
00:01:38,607 --> 00:01:41,195
or one litre, of cold water.

37
00:01:41,997 --> 00:01:44,146
Put the chicken in the water, and leave

38
00:01:44,156 --> 00:01:46,211
it for thirty minutes in the fridge.

39
00:01:47,013 --> 00:01:49,092
The salt helps the meat hold on to

40
00:01:49,102 --> 00:01:51,168
more moisture while it cooks.

41
00:01:51,831 --> 00:01:54,386
If you're short of time, skip the brine,

42
00:01:54,396 --> 00:01:57,695
and instead salt the chicken generously on
both

43
00:01:57,705 --> 00:02:00,235
sides fifteen minutes before cooking.

44
00:02:01,386 --> 00:02:03,709
Don't brine for more than an hour, or

45
00:02:03,719 --> 00:02:05,599
the texture can turn spongy.

46
00:02:06,262 --> 00:02:09,117
Raw chicken must always stay in the
fridge.

47
00:02:09,780 --> 00:02:12,022
Always use a clean bowl and wash it

48
00:02:12,032 --> 00:02:15,273
afterward with hot soapy water, since raw
chicken

49
00:02:15,283 --> 00:02:17,325
juices carry bacteria.

50
00:02:17,867 --> 00:02:18,888
Step three.

51
00:02:19,121 --> 00:02:21,433
Remove the chicken from the brine and pat

52
00:02:21,443 --> 00:02:23,938
it very dry with paper towels.

53
00:02:24,740 --> 00:02:27,700
Dry meat browns, wet meat steams.

54
00:02:28,502 --> 00:02:31,104
Don't rinse raw chicken under the tap,
because

55
00:02:31,114 --> 00:02:33,876
that splashes bacteria around your sink.

56
00:02:34,423 --> 00:02:37,104
Brush each side with a teaspoon of oil,

57
00:02:37,128 --> 00:02:41,353
and season with pepper, paprika, garlic
powder

58
00:02:41,482 --> 00:02:43,594
or any dry spices you like.

59
00:02:44,140 --> 00:02:47,332
If you skipped the brine, add salt now.

60
00:02:48,134 --> 00:02:50,272
Wash your hands and the board with hot

61
00:02:50,282 --> 00:02:51,918
soapy water afterward.

62
00:02:52,720 --> 00:02:56,530
Smoked paprika, garlic powder and dried
thyme make

63
00:02:56,540 --> 00:02:59,630
an easy all-purpose rub, with no sugar to

64
00:02:59,640 --> 00:03:01,020
burn in the pan.

65
00:03:01,567 --> 00:03:02,646
Step four.

66
00:03:03,100 --> 00:03:05,760
Heat a skillet over medium-high heat for
two

67
00:03:05,770 --> 00:03:08,683
minutes, then add a thin layer of oil.

68
00:03:09,230 --> 00:03:11,309
When it shimmers, lay the chicken in the

69
00:03:11,319 --> 00:03:13,942
pan, presentation side down.

70
00:03:14,396 --> 00:03:16,555
It should sizzle right away.

71
00:03:17,519 --> 00:03:19,854
Leave it alone for five to six minutes

72
00:03:19,864 --> 00:03:22,745
without moving it, until the underside is
a

73
00:03:22,755 --> 00:03:24,414
deep golden brown.

74
00:03:25,379 --> 00:03:26,829
Don't crowd the pan.

75
00:03:27,190 --> 00:03:30,742
If you're cooking more than two breasts,
work in batches.

76
00:03:31,195 --> 00:03:34,190
That browned crust is where the flavor
comes from.

77
00:03:34,737 --> 00:03:38,288
If the pan smokes heavily, lower the heat
slightly.

78
00:03:38,742 --> 00:03:42,816
A deep golden color is what you want, not
black.

79
00:03:43,367 --> 00:03:44,365
Step five.

80
00:03:44,726 --> 00:03:47,282
Flip the chicken with tongs, then turn the

81
00:03:47,292 --> 00:03:50,289
heat down to medium-low and cover the pan

82
00:03:50,299 --> 00:03:51,215
with a lid.

83
00:03:52,179 --> 00:03:55,385
The trapped steam finishes the cooking
gently, so

84
00:03:55,395 --> 00:03:58,367
the center cooks through without the
outside burning.

85
00:03:58,913 --> 00:04:03,312
Cook for another five to seven minutes,
depending on thickness.

86
00:04:03,859 --> 00:04:07,248
Don't keep lifting the lid, because the
heat escapes.

87
00:04:08,050 --> 00:04:10,896
A gentle finish is the difference between
juicy

88
00:04:10,906 --> 00:04:13,601
and dry chicken, so be patient and keep

89
00:04:13,611 --> 00:04:14,632
the heat low.

90
00:04:15,086 --> 00:04:17,433
If your breasts are very thin, three to

91
00:04:17,443 --> 00:04:20,762
four minutes will be enough, so start
checking early.

92
00:04:21,300 --> 00:04:22,356
Step six.

93
00:04:22,647 --> 00:04:23,714
Don't guess.

94
00:04:24,516 --> 00:04:27,571
Push an instant-read thermometer into the
thickest part

95
00:04:27,581 --> 00:04:30,367
of the breast, without touching the pan.

96
00:04:31,331 --> 00:04:34,352
Chicken is safe to eat at 165 degrees

97
00:04:34,362 --> 00:04:37,252
Fahrenheit, or 74 Celsius.

98
00:04:37,705 --> 00:04:39,507
Take the chicken out of the pan once

99
00:04:39,517 --> 00:04:42,409
it reaches that temperature, because it
keeps cooking

100
00:04:42,419 --> 00:04:44,009
a little as it rests.

101
00:04:44,671 --> 00:04:48,574
If it's below 165, cover the pan, and

102
00:04:48,584 --> 00:04:51,764
cook for a minute or two more, then check
again.

103
00:04:52,729 --> 00:04:55,596
Cutting into it to look is not reliable,

104
00:04:55,690 --> 00:04:57,778
and it lets the juices escape.

105
00:04:58,580 --> 00:05:00,637
Check a second breast as well if you

106
00:05:00,647 --> 00:05:03,447
are cooking several, because they never
finish at

107
00:05:03,457 --> 00:05:05,383
exactly the same time.

108
00:05:05,933 --> 00:05:07,174
Step seven.

109
00:05:08,324 --> 00:05:10,497
Move the chicken to a clean board or

110
00:05:10,507 --> 00:05:14,557
plate, and let it rest for five to ten
minutes.

111
00:05:15,708 --> 00:05:18,438
The juices relax and spread back through
the

112
00:05:18,448 --> 00:05:21,303
meat, instead of running out when you cut.

113
00:05:22,105 --> 00:05:24,890
Cover loosely with foil if your kitchen is
cool.

114
00:05:25,344 --> 00:05:28,341
Then slice across the grain, in slices
about

115
00:05:28,351 --> 00:05:29,546
half an inch thick.

116
00:05:30,510 --> 00:05:34,306
Serve in a salad, a sandwich or with
vegetables.

117
00:05:35,456 --> 00:05:38,346
Store leftovers in the fridge within two
hours,

118
00:05:38,405 --> 00:05:40,796
and eat within three to four days.

119
00:05:41,249 --> 00:05:43,317
Try the sliced chicken over a salad or

120
00:05:43,327 --> 00:05:46,624
inside a wrap for an easy lunch the next
day.

121
00:05:47,167 --> 00:05:49,177
If the chicken came out dry, you can

122
00:05:49,187 --> 00:05:50,313
still save dinner.

123
00:05:50,673 --> 00:05:53,078
Slice it thinly, and warm it for a

124
00:05:53,088 --> 00:05:54,341
minute in broth.

125
00:05:54,633 --> 00:05:57,232
You can also shred it for tacos or soup.

126
00:05:57,593 --> 00:06:00,216
If the center is pink, do not guess.

127
00:06:00,577 --> 00:06:03,075
Pink can be safe, and white can be

128
00:06:03,085 --> 00:06:05,870
raw, so trust only the thermometer.

129
00:06:06,672 --> 00:06:10,563
If it reads below 165 degrees Fahrenheit,
return

130
00:06:10,573 --> 00:06:11,652
it to the pan.

131
00:06:12,200 --> 00:06:14,997
A thermometer is only useful if it is
accurate.

132
00:06:15,231 --> 00:06:17,215
Test it in a glass of ice water:

133
00:06:17,448 --> 00:06:22,788
it should read 32 degrees Fahrenheit, or 0
Celsius.

134
00:06:23,335 --> 00:06:25,540
If it is off by a few degrees,

135
00:06:25,564 --> 00:06:28,547
adjust it if you can, or replace it.

136
00:06:29,209 --> 00:06:32,183
Slide the tip into the thickest part, away

137
00:06:32,193 --> 00:06:33,156
from the pan.

138
00:06:33,818 --> 00:06:35,965
Wait until the number stops moving.

139
00:06:36,930 --> 00:06:40,818
Wash the probe with hot soapy water after
each use.

140
00:06:41,367 --> 00:06:43,783
Spread the chicken in a shallow container
so

141
00:06:43,793 --> 00:06:47,298
it cools quickly, then cover it and
refrigerate.

142
00:06:47,752 --> 00:06:50,645
For longer storage, freeze it, and thaw it

143
00:06:50,655 --> 00:06:53,522
overnight in the fridge, never on the
counter.

144
00:06:54,184 --> 00:06:57,158
Reheat leftovers until they are steaming
hot all

145
00:06:57,168 --> 00:07:01,382
the way through, or 165 degrees Fahrenheit
again.

146
00:07:02,044 --> 00:07:04,484
Add a splash of water or broth, and

147
00:07:04,494 --> 00:07:07,848
cover the dish, so the meat stays tender.

148
00:07:08,400 --> 00:07:10,628
Here are the mistakes to avoid.

149
00:07:11,430 --> 00:07:14,785
First, cooking a thick, uneven breast.

150
00:07:15,935 --> 00:07:18,189
The thin part dries out before the thick

151
00:07:18,199 --> 00:07:19,347
part is safe.

152
00:07:19,708 --> 00:07:21,530
Even it out first.

153
00:07:22,680 --> 00:07:25,419
Second, cooking without a thermometer.

154
00:07:26,082 --> 00:07:28,661
Overcooking by only a few minutes can ruin

155
00:07:28,671 --> 00:07:32,025
the texture, and undercooking is unsafe.

156
00:07:32,316 --> 00:07:35,160
And third, slicing right away.

157
00:07:35,823 --> 00:07:38,550
Resting keeps the juices where they
belong.

158
00:07:39,700 --> 00:07:42,442
Do these three things right, and your
chicken

159
00:07:42,452 --> 00:07:44,169
will be tender every time.

160
00:07:44,530 --> 00:07:49,045
Keep it simple, trust the thermometer, and
enjoy the result.

161
00:07:49,600 --> 00:07:50,760
Let's recap.

162
00:07:51,910 --> 00:07:53,465
Even out the thickness.

163
00:07:53,826 --> 00:07:55,346
Brine for moisture.

164
00:07:56,496 --> 00:07:58,272
Dry and season well.

165
00:07:58,819 --> 00:08:00,548
Sear in a hot pan.

166
00:08:01,698 --> 00:08:04,507
Flip, cover and lower the heat.

167
00:08:05,471 --> 00:08:09,301
Check with a thermometer for 165 degrees.

168
00:08:09,755 --> 00:08:12,854
And rest the chicken, then slice across
the grain.

169
00:08:13,819 --> 00:08:17,234
Seven steps, about thirty minutes of
cooking, and

170
00:08:17,244 --> 00:08:19,309
chicken breast that stays juicy.

171
00:08:20,460 --> 00:08:24,070
Bonus sections cover rescuing dry or pink
chicken,

172
00:08:24,245 --> 00:08:28,528
checking your thermometer, and storing
leftovers safely.

173
00:08:29,067 --> 00:08:32,224
That's how you cook chicken breast without
drying it out.

174
00:08:32,585 --> 00:08:36,160
If dinner was juicy tonight, subscribe to
WikiTube,

175
00:08:36,219 --> 00:08:39,748
because we publish a new how-to every
single day.

176
00:08:40,201 --> 00:08:42,014
Tell us in the comments how you season

177
00:08:42,024 --> 00:08:44,116
your chicken, and what you would like us

178
00:08:44,126 --> 00:08:45,831
to explain next.

179
00:08:46,982 --> 00:08:48,072
See you tomorrow.

180
00:08:48,735 --> 00:08:52,115
Next time, try different spices, because
the method

181
00:08:52,125 --> 00:08:54,295
stays exactly the same.

182
00:08:54,400 --> 00:08:55,572
That's WikiTube.

183
00:08:55,805 --> 00:08:58,080
Whatever it is, here's how.
